          "t": "p",
          "text": "The finding the authors put first, though, is not about hormones. It is that the women reported a general lack of awareness that perimenopause was happening at all — and that not knowing made everything worse. Uncertainty fed the anxiety, and the anxiety fed a sense of having lost control of a body that had stopped behaving predictably. If that sounds familiar, it matches [the US survey that found one in three women over 35 can't tell whether they're in perimenopause](/blog/perimenopause-uncertainty-us-study/). Twenty women recruited from support groups is not a representative sample of anything, and the researchers say so; it is a description, not a prevalence estimate."
