          "text": "It will be, some nights. The two conditions do not take turns, and there is no reason a flush cannot land on a night your glucose is also drifting down. The guidance for that is unambiguous and worth stating on its own line: treat the low first. A hot flush is miserable and it is not dangerous. An untreated low is the other way round. The order of operations is not a close call."
