              "detail": "Stated by ASPS member surgeons in a consumer-facing article on oestrogen-based medical skincare: “women can lose up to 30 percent of their dermal collagen within the first five years after menopause, followed by an additional 2 percent decline each year.” The article also sets out oestrogen’s role in collagen production, dermal thickness, elasticity, hyaluronic acid and barrier function. This is expert summary rather than a citation to a specific study — treat the figure as an order of magnitude.",
              "cite": "American Society of Plastic Surgeons · Expert article",
              "url": "https://www.plasticsurgery.org/news/articles/the-innovation-of-estrogen-based-medical-skincare"
